# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# Plan 00208 Phase 3: a failed Ctrl+Insert/Alt+Insert (Claude) dictation now shows its
# notification even with Show Notifications off, as does every failure notice that stays
# (wsi, wsi-stream, wsi-article; an article stopped at its silence or duration limit now
# notifies too). Builds and installs the new wsi-postprocess, and deploys the extension's new
# menu items, Post-Process Last Transcription: Corporate and Natural (the result goes to the
# clipboard, the transcription stays as it was), and a notification at login if a record key
# could not be registered. THE EXTENSION CHANGED: LOG OUT AND BACK IN after this run (Wayland
# reloads extension code only at login); the scripts and binaries apply at once.
# Plan 00208 Phase 4: builds and installs wsi-claude-token, which wsi-claude-process now asks
# for the Claude account. Settings gains "Use the token with the most allowance left" (off by
# default, so nothing changes until it is ticked): each post-processing then runs as the token
# with the most 5-hour and weekly allowance left, read with ccy --token-usage (one small request
# per token, cached 15 minutes). When none has any left it fails, the notification names each
# token and its reset, and the panel shows an amber warning icon and a menu item to clear it.
# THE EXTENSION CHANGED AGAIN (extension.js, prefs.js, the schema, the new tokenWarning.js):
# LOG OUT AND BACK IN after this run.
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-speech-to-text.yml
